---
// Lesson 1.7's "Watch it learn" (its brief, Interactive) on the shared shell (p6 D2). Every dot, line, ring, word and
// point is worked out here at build time by src/lib/watch-it-learn.ts from data/interactive/watch-it-learn.json. The
// script computes nothing: each press of Back or Next round shows another round, and nothing moves by itself.
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { ends, learnData, watchItLearn, where } from '../lib/watch-it-learn.ts';
import Shell from './Shell.astro';

const data = learnData.parse(JSON.parse(readFileSync('data/interactive/watch-it-learn.json', 'utf8')));
const { dots, rounds, closest } = watchItLearn(data);
const L = data.limit;
const last = rounds.length - 1;
// The brief's drawing rules: the dot chart from (10, 10) to (310, 310); the "How wrong" chart 320 by 120.
const X = (x: number) => +(10 + (x + L) * 30).toFixed(2);
const Y = (y: number) => +(310 - (y + L) * 30).toFixed(2);
const edge = (w: [number, number, number]) => {
  const [[, x1, y1], [, x2, y2]] = ends(w, L);
  return { x1: X(x1), y1: Y(y1), x2: X(x2), y2: Y(y2) };
};
const L0 = Math.max(rounds[0].loss, rounds[0].newLoss);
const points = (key: 'loss' | 'newLoss', r: number) => rounds.slice(0, r + 1).map((o) => `${20 + 28 * o.r},${+(110 - (100 * o[key]) / L0).toFixed(2)}`).join(' ');
const CHOICES = [
  ['A', 'Line A slopes down from the top left to the bottom right.', 'You picked line A.'],
  ['B', 'Line B is flat, across the middle.', 'You picked line B.'],
  ['C', 'Line C is upright, down the middle.', 'You picked line C.'],
  ['', 'I am not sure.', 'You were not sure.'],
];
const DASH: Record<string, string> = { A: '8 4', B: '2 4', C: '12 4 2 4' };
const letters = Object.entries(data.candidates);
const setup = `The thick line is the model's first try. ${where(data.start, L)}`;
const name = (r: number) => `${rounds[r].words} ${rounds[r].where}`;
const at = (i: number) => ({ cx: X(dots[i].x), cy: Y(dots[i].y) });
// The brief's one sentence; true while T4 and T5 in src/lib/watch-it-learn.test.ts pass.
const SENTENCE = "Each round changed the model's numbers and moved the line: in the end, fewer dots were wrong, but not none.";
---

<Shell title="Watch it learn" reveal="Start training" class="watch-it-learn">
  <p>These dots are made up for this lesson. Each dot is an example.</p>
  <p>Circles and squares are two groups. A model will learn to split them with a straight line.</p>
  {/* Design run 33 D4 (Emanuel, 28-09-26): the start line alone, named on the chart; each choice has its own picture. */}
  <svg viewBox="0 0 320 320" role="img" aria-label={setup} data-chart="setup">
    <rect x="10" y="10" width="300" height="300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" />
    <g fill="currentColor">{dots.map((d, i) => !d.new && (d.square ? <rect data-dot={i} x={at(i).cx - 6} y={at(i).cy - 6} width="12" height="12" /> : <circle data-dot={i} {...at(i)} r="6" />))}</g>
    <line data-line="start" {...edge(data.start)} stroke-width="3" />
    <text x="302" y={edge(data.start).y2 + 42} text-anchor="end">The model's first try</text>
  </svg>
  <p>The thick line is the model's first try. It is in the wrong place. Each round of training moves it a little.</p>
  <p class="as-text">{CHOICES.slice(0, 3).map((c) => c[1]).join(' ')} Where will the line end up? The answer is below, so decide first if you want to guess.</p>
  <fieldset class="pictures">
    <legend>Which picture shows where the line will end up?</legend>
    {
      CHOICES.map(([value, label, said]) => (
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="wil-pick" value={value} data-said={said} />
          {value && (
            <svg viewBox="0 0 320 320" aria-hidden="true" class="pick">
              <rect x="10" y="10" width="300" height="300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" />
              <g fill="currentColor">{dots.map((d, i) => !d.new && (d.square ? <rect data-dot={i} x={at(i).cx - 6} y={at(i).cy - 6} width="12" height="12" /> : <circle data-dot={i} {...at(i)} r="6" />))}</g>
              <line data-line={value} {...edge(data.candidates[value])} stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray={DASH[value]} vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" />
            </svg>
          )}
          {label}
        </label>
      ))
    }
  </fieldset>
  <p>There is no wrong guess here.</p>
  <Fragment slot="after">
    <p>Squares go above the line. Circles go below it. A ring means the dot is on the wrong side.</p>
    <p data-layer="deep">Hollow dots are new dots. The model did not learn from them.</p>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 320 320" role="img" aria-label={name(last)} data-chart="dots">
      <rect x="10" y="10" width="300" height="300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" />
      {dots.map((d, i) => (
        <g data-layer={d.new ? 'deep' : undefined} fill={d.new ? 'none' : 'currentColor'}>
          {d.square ? <rect data-dot={i} x={at(i).cx - 6} y={at(i).cy - 6} width="12" height="12" /> : <circle data-dot={i} {...at(i)} r="6" />}
        </g>
      ))}
      {letters.map(([k, c]) => (
        <g data-pick={k} display="none" stroke-opacity="0.6">
          <line {...edge(c)} stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray={DASH[k]} />
          <text x={edge(c).x2 - 14} y={edge(c).y2 - 6}>{k}</text>
        </g>
      ))}
      {rounds.map((o) => (
        <g data-round={o.r} data-last={o.r === last ? '' : undefined} class:list={[{ now: !o.r }]} data-wrong={o.wrong.join(' ')} data-new-wrong={o.newWrong.join(' ')} data-w={o.w.join(' ')}>
          <line {...edge(o.w)} stroke-width="3" />
          {o.wrong.map((i) => <circle data-ring={i} {...at(i)} r="11" />)}
          <g data-layer="deep">{o.newWrong.map((i) => <circle data-ring={i} {...at(i)} r="11" />)}</g>
        </g>
      ))}
    </svg>
    <p class="legend">Solid line: the model's line. <span data-key hidden>Dashed line: your guess.</span></p>
    <div class="rounds">
      {
        rounds.map((o) => (
          <div data-round={o.r} data-last={o.r === last ? '' : undefined} class:list={[{ now: !o.r }]}>
            <p>{o.words}</p>
            <p>{o.where}</p>
            {o.deep && <p data-layer="deep">{o.deep}</p>}
            {o.r === last && (
              <Fragment>
                <p>This was the last round. Training stopped here.</p>
                <p>The line ended up closest to line {closest}. <span data-picked></span></p>
                <p>{SENTENCE}</p>
                <p>We made these dots up, and we chose where the line starts, so you can see it move.</p>
                <p>Lesson 1.8 shows how a chatbot uses the earlier words in a chat.</p>
                <p data-layer="deep">Both lines fell, round by round. If the dashed line had started to rise, that would suggest overfitting.</p>
              </Fragment>
            )}
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="sr" aria-live="polite" data-live></p>
    <button type="button" data-turn="-1" aria-disabled="true">Back</button>
    <button type="button" data-turn="1">Next round</button>
    <h3>How wrong the guesses are</h3>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 320 120" role="img" aria-label={name(last)} data-chart="loss">
      <text x="30" y="12">More wrong</text>
      <text x="4" y="118">Less wrong</text>
      <text x="316" y="118" text-anchor="end">Rounds</text>
      {
        rounds.map((o) => (
          <g data-round={o.r} data-last={o.r === last ? '' : undefined} class:list={[{ now: !o.r }]}>
            <polyline data-loss="example" points={points('loss', o.r)} stroke-width="2" />
            <polyline data-loss="new" data-layer="deep" points={points('newLoss', o.r)} stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />
            <circle fill="currentColor" cx={20 + 28 * o.r} cy={+(110 - (100 * o.loss) / L0).toFixed(2)} r="3" />
          </g>
        ))
      }
    </svg>
    <p data-layer="deep">Solid line: the example dots. Dashed line: the new dots.</p>
  </Fragment>
</Shell>

<script>
  // One round at a time, by button only: the round's groups show, its words go to the live region and name both charts.
  for (const box of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.watch-it-learn')) {
    const groups = [...box.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-round]')];
    const end = Math.max(...groups.map((g) => Number(g.dataset.round)));
    const said = box.querySelector('[data-live]');
    const [back, next] = box.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-turn]');
    let round = 0;
    const show = () => {
      for (const g of groups) g.classList.toggle('now', Number(g.dataset.round) === round);
      const [words, where] = [...box.querySelectorAll(`.rounds [data-round="${round}"] p`)].map((p) => p.textContent);
      for (const chart of box.querySelectorAll('[data-chart="dots"], [data-chart="loss"]')) chart.setAttribute('aria-label', `${words} ${where}`);
      back.setAttribute('aria-disabled', String(round === 0));
      next.setAttribute('aria-disabled', String(round === end));
      return words;
    };
    for (const turn of [back, next])
      turn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const to = round + Number(turn.dataset.turn);
        if (to >= 0 && to <= end) round = to;
        if (said) said.textContent = to < 0 ? 'This is the start, before training.' : to > end ? 'This is the last round.' : show();
      });
    // The reveal says round 0's words (brief, screen 3).
    box.querySelector('[data-reveal]')?.addEventListener('click', () => said && (said.textContent = show()));
    box.addEventListener('change', (e) => {
      const input = e.target as HTMLInputElement;
      for (const g of box.querySelectorAll('[data-pick]')) g.setAttribute('display', g.getAttribute('data-pick') === input.value ? 'inline' : 'none');
      const key = box.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-key]');
      if (key) key.hidden = !input.value;
      const picked = box.querySelector('[data-picked]');
      if (picked) picked.textContent = input.dataset.said ?? '';
    });
    show();
  }
</script>
